WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.210
On India's west coast, on the Arabian Sea,

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.830
a great city stands on a
group of former islands.

3
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.830
In 2000, the UN put its
population at 16.0 million.

4
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.350
By 2025, 20.2 million.

5
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:19.050
It is the world's densest
city of a million or more:

6
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.050
27,000 people per square kilometre.

7
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.470
And people keep arriving
from villages across India.

8
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.150
So when a city grows this
fast, who really gains?

9
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.650
In this mission, you'll
find out why Mumbai matters,

10
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.950
to India and to the world.

11
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.910
Then you'll weigh up what that
growth offers the people who arrive.

12
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.920
Your mission: decide who really
gains from Mumbai's growth.
